{
  "_doc": {
    "about": "Calendar invites every client must match: web (shared/src/calendar.ts, ical.js) and Android :core. iCalendar texts are given as `lines`, joined with CRLF and ended with CRLF; lines starting with a space are folded continuations. All people and addresses are made up.",
    "parse": "parseCalendar(text, defaultTimeZone) → { method (upper-case or null), events } or null when it isn't iCalendar or has no VEVENT with DTSTART. Times: VALUE=DATE → { kind: 'date', date: 'yyyy-mm-dd' }; 'Z' → { kind: 'dateTime', utc, timeZone: 'UTC' }; TZID with a VTIMEZONE of that TZID in the part → resolved by it, timeZone = ianaZone(TZID); TZID without one → the wall time in ianaZone(TZID) (an IANA name, or a Windows name from WINDOWS_ZONES), or defaultTimeZone when it names neither, timeZone = ianaZone(TZID) (null when none); no TZID and no Z (floating) → wall time in defaultTimeZone, timeZone null. A wall time the clock repeats takes the earlier instant; one it skips moves forward by the gap (java.time ZonedDateTime.of). utc is ISO 8601 to the second with Z. end: DTEND, else DTSTART + DURATION, else the next day for a date, else the start (same TZID as DTSTART). Text values are unescaped and trimmed; missing ones are ''. People: email = the EMAIL parameter if it is a plain address, else the value without 'mailto:' (case-insensitive) if that is one (plain address: exactly one '@' with text on each side; no whitespace, control characters, ',', ';', '<' or '>'); an organizer with neither is null (no RSVP by mail), an attendee with neither is left out; name = CN, or '' when missing or equal to the email (case-insensitive). Attendee partstat/role/kind(CUTYPE) upper-case, defaults NEEDS-ACTION, REQ-PARTICIPANT, INDIVIDUAL; rsvp = RSVP is TRUE. sequence defaults to 0; status upper-case or null. recurrence = recurrenceText(RRULE, start's timeZone or defaultTimeZone) or null. A VTIMEZONE STANDARD/DAYLIGHT RRULE whose FREQ isn't YEARLY is ignored (the observance applies from its DTSTART on), so a hostile rule can't stall parsing; a VEVENT that can't be read is skipped.",
    "recurrence": "recurrenceText(rrule, timeZone). FREQ DAILY/WEEKLY/MONTHLY/YEARLY → 'Daily'/'Weekly'/'Monthly'/'Annually', or with INTERVAL n > 1 'Every n days/weeks/months/years'; any other FREQ → 'Repeats'. WEEKLY with BYDAY: ' on weekdays' for exactly MO–FR, else ' on ' + day names joined 'A, B and C' in the order given. MONTHLY: BYMONTHDAY=n → ' on day n'; BYMONTHDAY=-1 → ' on the last day'; one BYDAY with a position (1..5, -1), or with BYSETPOS → ' on the first|second|third|fourth|fifth|last Dayname'. Then COUNT → ', once' or ', n times'; else UNTIL → ', until Mon d, yyyy' (English short month; a UTC UNTIL as its date in timeZone).",
    "reply": "buildReply({ event (parsed from the named invite, its event at index `event`), attendee, partstat, now, comment }); see shared/src/calendar.ts. Lines, in order: BEGIN:VCALENDAR, PRODID:-//hafa.cc//Inbox//EN, VERSION:2.0, CALSCALE:GREGORIAN, METHOD:REPLY, BEGIN:VEVENT, DTSTART and DTEND (UTC 'yyyymmddThhmmssZ', or ';VALUE=DATE:yyyymmdd'), DTSTAMP (now, UTC, seconds truncated), ORGANIZER[;CN=…]:mailto:…, UID (TEXT escaped like SUMMARY), RECURRENCE-ID (when the event has one, same form as DTSTART), ATTENDEE;PARTSTAT=…[;CN=…]:mailto:…, COMMENT (when non-blank, trimmed and escaped), SEQUENCE, SUMMARY (TEXT escaped: backslash, semicolon and comma get a backslash, line breaks become \\n), END:VEVENT, END:VCALENDAR. CN: quotes and line breaks dropped, then in double quotes when it holds : ; or ,; left out when the name is empty. Lines folded at 75 octets (74 after the first piece, plus the leading space), never inside a UTF-8 sequence; CRLF after every line. replyMail: to = organizer, subject 'Accepted: ' / 'Tentatively accepted: ' / 'Declined: ' + summary, with every run of whitespace (line breaks too) as one space and trimmed, markdown '<name or email> has accepted|tentatively accepted|declined this invitation.' plus a blank line and the trimmed comment when there is one.",
    "fold": "foldLine(line): pieces joined by CRLF + space; the first at most 75 octets, the rest at most 74 plus the space; a character is never split.",
    "mime": "buildMime with calendar { method, content }: a third alternative part after text/html: 'Content-Type: text/calendar; charset=UTF-8; method=<method>', 'Content-Transfer-Encoding: base64', body base64 of the UTF-8 content in 76-character lines.",
    "replyRefused": "buildReply (and replyMail when it is the organizer's) must throw InvalidAddressError (Android: its typed error) when the organizer's or attendee's address isn't a plain address; fields as in reply."
  },
